156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Continuation from YTAC or ICIA: Projects submitted for IITS may continue from those used in YTAC or ICIA. However, if your team composition changes by more than one member, the project must be a new submission for IITS to ensure compliance with intellectual property rights. The organisers will strictly enforce this rule, and any projects that do not adhere to it will be disqualified without a refund.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Judging and Appeals: The organisers reserve full rights in judging the projects, and all decisions made by the judges are final. No appeals or reconsiderations will be entertained after the judgment has been made.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (5. Investment Agreements: Any investment agreements arising from the projects are solely between the investors and the participants. The organisers will not be involved in, nor take responsibility for, any investment-related matters.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (6. Documentation Requirements: Each project submission must include comprehensive documentation, including an A1 size poster , and a business plan outlining potential market applications. This documentation is critical for the evaluation process and must be submitted by the specified deadline.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 495 0 R
/ActualText (7. Presentation and Demonstration: All teams must prepare a presentation and live demonstration of their project. The presentation should clearly articulate the problem addressed, the innovation introduced, and the potential market impact. Teams will be required to demonstrate the functionality of their prototype during the judging process.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 496 0 R
/ActualText (8. Submission Format and Deadline Adherence: All submissions must be in digital format, including source code, designs, and any other relevant files, and must be submitted through the designated online portal. All project submissions, including any required documentation and files, must be submitted by the specified deadline. Late submissions will result in disqualification, and any logistics fees or payments made will not be refunded.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 497 0 R
/ActualText (9. Team Size and Composition: Each team must consist of 1 to 3 members. Changes to team composition after submission are not allowed unless specifically approved by the organizers.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (10. Compliance with Ethical Standards: Projects must adhere to ethical standards, including respect for intellectual property rights, data privacy, and the avoidance of harmful or controversial content. Projects found to violate these standards will be disqualified.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 498 0 R
